---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import StatGrid from '../../components/StatGrid.astro';
import BeforeAfterTable from '../../components/BeforeAfterTable.astro';
import CaseSidebar from '../../components/CaseSidebar.astro';

/* Breadcrumb "Case studies" renders as plain text — there is no listing
   page yet, and dead links are intentionally not ported. */
---

<Base title="How Ledgerline cut fraud review time from 4 hours to 90 seconds">
  <div class="cs-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumb">
        <a href="/">Platform</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>Case studies</span>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span style="color:#fff">Ledgerline</span>
      </div>
      <h1>How Ledgerline cut fraud review time from <em>4 hours to 90 seconds</em></h1>
      <div class="cs-kpis">
        <div class="cs-kpi"><span class="v g">-62%</span><span class="l">False positives</span></div>
        <div class="cs-kpi"><span class="v">90s</span><span class="l">Median resolution</span></div>
        <div class="cs-kpi"><span class="v">$1.4M</span><span class="l">Recovered revenue / yr</span></div>
        <div class="cs-kpi"><span class="v">2.1M</span><span class="l">Decisions / month</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cs-body">
    <div class="wrap cs-layout">
      <article>
        <p class="summary">
          Ledgerline, a payments processor handling <strong>2.1 million monthly transactions</strong>,
          was losing good customers to a fraud queue that took four hours to clear.
          After a six-week evaluation, they replaced their rules engine and a prompted-LLM
          pilot with Verdict — cutting median review time to <strong>90 seconds</strong>,
          reducing false positives by <strong>62%</strong>, and recovering
          <strong>$1.4M in annual revenue</strong> that had been leaking to over-blocking.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="pull">
          <p>“We weren't choosing a model. We were choosing whether our analysts would still have a job in two years — and whether our good customers would still be here.”</p>
          <cite><b>Dana Whitfield</b> · VP Risk Operations, Ledgerline</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="cs-section">
          <span class="lbl">01 — Situation</span>
          <h3>A queue that grew faster than the team</h3>
          <p>
            Ledgerline's risk team had 14 analysts working a queue of roughly 9,000 flagged
            transactions per day. Each review took a median of four hours end-to-end, and
            the backlog meant most cases were resolved long after the customer had already
            abandoned the purchase.
          </p>
          <p>
            The cost wasn't just operational. Roughly one in five holds turned out to be a
            legitimate customer — and Ledgerline's own data showed that a customer who
            experiences a fraud hold is <b>3.4× more likely</b> to churn within 90 days.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-section">
          <span class="lbl">02 — Evaluation</span>
          <h3>Four options, three criteria that mattered</h3>
          <p>
            The team spent six weeks evaluating four approaches. They were explicit about
            what would make them walk away:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><b>p99 latency under 200ms.</b> Anything slower couldn't sit inline in the authorization path — it would have to stay async, which defeats the purpose.</li>
            <li><b>No hallucinated output formats.</b> The downstream system parses a strict schema. A single malformed response at 3am pages an on-call engineer.</li>
            <li><b>Adding a new decline reason without retraining.</b> Their fraud taxonomy changed roughly every six weeks. A model that needed a training cycle for each change was a non-starter.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            A prompted LLM passed the flexibility test but failed on latency (p99 ~6.4s) and
            output reliability (71% parseable in their harness). Expanding the rules engine
            passed latency but failed the adaptability test — the rule tree was already
            4,000 branches deep. A fine-tuned classifier passed latency and reliability but
            required a retraining cycle for every taxonomy change.
          </p>
          <p>
            Verdict was the only option that cleared all three criteria in the pilot.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-section">
          <span class="lbl">03 — Result</span>
          <h3>Ninety seconds, and a queue that clears itself</h3>
          <p>
            Ledgerline deployed Verdict inside their own VPC, inline in the authorization
            path. Low-confidence decisions still escalate to a human — but that's now
            roughly <b>8% of volume</b> instead of 100%.
          </p>

          <StatGrid items={[
            { v: '-62%', l: 'False positives in the first 90 days' },
            { v: '90s', l: 'Median time to resolution' },
            { v: '8%', l: 'Volume still escalated to humans' },
          ]} />

          <p>
            The team also stopped shipping rule changes through engineering. Risk analysts
            now modify the options array directly through a config surface — the fraud
            taxonomy has changed five times since launch with no model retraining and no
            deployment.
          </p>

          <BeforeAfterTable
            headers={['Metric', 'Before', 'After']}
            rows={[
              { name: 'Median resolution time', before: '4h 12m', after: '1m 30s' },
              { name: 'False positive rate', before: '19.4%', after: '7.4%' },
              { name: 'Cost per decision', before: '$0.86', after: '$0.04' },
              { name: 'Taxonomy change cycle', before: '6 weeks', after: 'Same day' },
              { name: 'Analyst headcount on queue', before: '14', after: '4' },
              { name: 'p99 decision latency', before: '6,400ms', after: '140ms' },
            ]}
          />

          <p>
            The 10 analysts who moved off the queue were redeployed to complex case
            investigation — work that had been perpetually deprioritized. Ledgerline
            reports that the team now closes roughly <b>3× more high-value investigations</b>
            per quarter than before the migration.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-section">
          <span class="lbl">Next</span>
          <h3>See how this works for fraud triage</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom:22px">
            Bring a sample of your own flagged transactions and define your option set.
            You'll get a calibration report before you talk to anyone.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/roi-calculator/">Estimate your savings →</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#architecture">Read the architecture paper</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <CaseSidebar />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .cs-hero {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 70px 0 74px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cs-hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(800px 400px at 82% 0%, rgba(0, 200, 150, 0.14), transparent 62%);
  }
  .cs-hero .wrap {
    position: relative;
  }
  .cs-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    max-width: 880px;
    margin-bottom: 34px;
    line-height: 1.12;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .cs-hero h1 em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--mint);
  }
  .cs-kpis {
    display: flex;
    gap: 52px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding-top: 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
  }
  .cs-kpi .v {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    display: block;
  }
  .cs-kpi .v.g {
    color: var(--mint);
  }
  .cs-kpi .l {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: #7c87a3;
    margin-top: 5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .cs-body {
    padding: 64px 0;
  }
  .cs-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 296px;
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .summary {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.66;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 480;
    padding: 26px 0 34px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  }
  .summary strong {
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  blockquote.pull {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 6px 0 6px 26px;
    margin: 0 0 44px;
  }
  blockquote.pull p {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  blockquote.pull cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: block;
    font-weight: 560;
  }
  blockquote.pull cite b {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 660;
  }
  .cs-section {
    margin-bottom: 52px;
  }
  .cs-section .lbl {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    display: block;
  }
  .cs-section h3 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .cs-section p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #39415a;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .cs-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .cs-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .cs-section ul li {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    color: #39415a;
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding-left: 26px;
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: 11px;
  }
  .cs-section ul li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .cs-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 44px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .cs-kpis {
      gap: 30px;
    }
    .cs-hero h1 {
      font-size: 26px;
    }
  }
</style>
